\f0\b0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \uc0\u8232 \cb3 Students will step into the role of a communication strategist responding to a real-time business crisis. Through a scenario-based simulation, they will practice making quick but thoughtful decisions about messaging, tone, stakeholders, and timing. This activity is designed to strengthen your ability to manage high-stakes communication, align responses with organizational values, and protect brand credibility\'97all essential leadership skills in moments of uncertainty.\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cf7 \strokec7 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\b \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 Learning Activities
\f0\b0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\b \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb3 1) Read and listen to Public Leadership Through Crisis:
\f0\b0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \'a0In this podcast, crisis expert Shruti Mehrotra shares leadership lessons from global crisis zones. She emphasizes disciplined decision-making, trusted teams, remote expertise, and the importance of rest. Using models like the \'93snowflake structure,\'94 she urges leaders to balance urgent action with long-term thinking\'97and to see crisis as a chance to build something better.\'a0\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\b \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb3 2) Read 1 Big Thing: How American Airlines Communicated Through Tragedy:\'a0
\f0\b0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 After a deadly midair collision, American Airlines responded quickly with clear, empathetic communication. Their disciplined crisis plan, timely updates, and focus on facts helped maintain public trust during a high-stakes tragedy.\'a0\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\b \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 \cb3 3) Read Public Relations Society of America (PRSA) Code of Ethics:\'a0
\f0\b0 \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 The PRSA Code of Ethics outlines the core values and principles that guide ethical practice in the public relations profession. Designed to promote integrity, transparency, and public trust, the Code helps PR professionals navigate real-world challenges by emphasizing responsible advocacy, honesty, and fairness. It serves as both a standard of excellence and a practical tool for ethical decision-making.\'a0\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \cb3 4)\'a0
\f1\b \AppleTypeServices\AppleTypeServicesF65539 Optional Assignment: Reputation Recovery Brief (you do not turn this in; however, it helps prepare you for the Milestone and Final Assessment).
